    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="examples_1md_src_2examples"/></para>
<para>This page documents the <computeroutput>C</computeroutput> versions of the example simulations used in the NDXL publication, together illustrating the capabilities of NDXL. For a brief introductory example using the Kuramoto model, see the <bold><ulink url="https://github.com/NonlinearC/NDXL/tree/main/NDXL">NDXL source repository</ulink></bold>. We recommend reading through the <ref refid="installation" kindref="compound">Installation</ref> guide before writing any code, as this section assumes a similar file structure, and that call source code is placed in <computeroutput>main.c</computeroutput>. We also strongly recommend first reading through the <ref refid="concepts" kindref="compound">Concepts</ref> page, as we will assume you are familiar with the network dynamics-specific terminology.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This is NOT a replacement for the <bold><ulink url="topics.html">API documentation</ulink></bold>, which provides detailed explanations on functions, objects, and typedefs used. The sections should be absorbed in tandem.</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="examples_1autotoc_md20">
<title>Getting Started</title><para>All NDXL programs <bold>MUST</bold> call <ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit()</ref> before any NDXL functionality. This function initialises crucial internal variables, and registers garbage collection functions that automatically and safely release any remaining NDXL objects when the program terminates.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>The garbage collection in NDXL handles <bold>only</bold> memory allocated by NDXL. Any memory alloctaed by the user using e.g., <computeroutput>malloc()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>calloc()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>realloc()</computeroutput>, must still be manually released by the user using <computeroutput>free()</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
The core object in NDXL is a <ref refid="group__ndxl__network" kindref="compound">NDXLNetwork</ref> <ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>, which is a (initially empty) host object for creating vertices, edges, and noise channels, and which later becomes the target of <ref refid="group__network__simulation" kindref="compound">simulation</ref> functions. We will start by defining an empty network using <ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork()</ref>, which takes in a single parameter, a <computeroutput>void*</computeroutput> containing any extra data we want the network to use. We will pass <computeroutput>0</computeroutput> for now, since we do not yet have any data the network should rely on.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>*<sp/>nwk<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork</ref>(0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>We now need to populate <computeroutput>nwk</computeroutput> with some vertices, so that we have components to simulate. Each vertex needs a <ref refid="group__vertex__dnc_1ga1140d9424f744e76f6ae10fde2d3329e" kindref="member">dynamics function</ref> that describes how its state vector evolves over time <formula id="13">$t$</formula>, expressed as a time ordinary differential equations (ODE). For example, if we want a vertex wtih state vector <formula id="14">$\vec{x}$</formula> to evolve according to</para>
<para><formula id="15">\[\frac{d\vec{x}}{dt} = A\vec{x}t
\]</formula></para>
<para>where <formula id="7">$A$</formula> is some constant, and <formula id="14">$\vec{x}$</formula> has one element (is a scalar), then in NDXL we write:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>dynamics(<ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref>*<sp/>vertex,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>dx,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>x,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>t,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>params)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>A<sp/>=<sp/>*(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal">*)params;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dx[0]<sp/>=<sp/>A<sp/>*<sp/>x[0]<sp/>*<sp/>t;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The <computeroutput>//...</computeroutput> comments are used to indicate &quot;same as before&quot;.</para>
</simplesect>
In our function, we exctract <formula id="7">$A$</formula> from the user-defined <computeroutput>void* params</computeroutput> that we will pass to the vertex constructor, and we write the differential equation in-place to the output vector <computeroutput>dx</computeroutput>. In <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput>, we can now create the vertex, baring in mind that whatever <computeroutput>void* params</computeroutput> points to must persist in memory for the lifetime of the vertex, as NDXL does not copy these data.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>*<sp/>nwk<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork</ref>(0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Create<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>A,<sp/>and<sp/>initial<sp/>conditions<sp/>x0</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>A<sp/>=<sp/>2.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>x0<sp/>=<sp/>1.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Create<sp/>vertex<sp/>on<sp/>`nwk`</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref>*<sp/>vert<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__creation_1gaec4b6881830464281fc35817e96bfaf3" kindref="member">ndxlCreateVertex</ref>(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>nwk,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Host<sp/>network</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&amp;x0,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Initial<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>-<sp/>must<sp/>be<sp/>a<sp/>pointer<sp/>to<sp/>double</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>1,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Length<sp/>of<sp/>state<sp/>vector</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>dynamics,<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Dynamics<sp/>function<sp/>the<sp/>vertex<sp/>state<sp/>must<sp/>evolve<sp/>according<sp/>to</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>NULL,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>No<sp/>noise<sp/>function<sp/>(see<sp/>@ref<sp/>sde)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>NULL,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>No<sp/>noise<sp/>channels<sp/>(must<sp/>be<sp/>NULL<sp/>if<sp/>noise<sp/>function<sp/>is<sp/>NULL)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>0,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Number<sp/>of<sp/>noise<sp/>channels<sp/>(must<sp/>be<sp/>0<sp/>if<sp/>noise<sp/>function<sp/>is<sp/>NULL)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>NULL,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>No<sp/>discrete<sp/>callback</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&amp;A<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>User-defined<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>We could now simulate <computeroutput>nwk</computeroutput>, but we have no way of retrieving the simulated outputs, as NDXL does not automatically store these. To capture simulation output, we use a <ref refid="group__network__callbacks" kindref="compound">discrete callback</ref> that operates on the network object. Here, we will write the state vector of <computeroutput>vert</computeroutput> out to a CSV file at each evaluated time step.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;stdio.h&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>cb(<ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>*<sp/>net,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>time,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>params)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>FILE*<sp/>csvfile<sp/>=<sp/>(FILE*)params;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref>*<sp/>vertex<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__traversal_1ga654f02fad350c904b773221e86d687a8" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkFirstVertex</ref>(net);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>x<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__vertex__functions_1ga1f59cebd8575f89020b590ba036006c8" kindref="member">ndxlVertexState</ref>(vertex)[0];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fprintf(csvfile,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;%f,%f\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>time,<sp/>x);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Because the network only has one vertex, <ref refid="group__network__traversal_1ga654f02fad350c904b773221e86d687a8" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkFirstVertex()</ref> will give us the corresponding <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> pointer. Since this pointer is shared, we do not need to (and SHOULD NOT) release the associated reosources after we are done using it. Here, the <computeroutput>void* params</computeroutput> refers to the parameters pointer associated with the network, which, if you&apos;ll recall from earlier, we set to <computeroutput>0</computeroutput>! We therefore need to modify our network creation to have the output file as its <computeroutput>void* params</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;stdio.h&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Create<sp/>file<sp/>handle,<sp/>and<sp/>write<sp/>column<sp/>headers<sp/>if<sp/>successful</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>FILE*<sp/>f_output<sp/>=<sp/>fopen(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;states.csv&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;w&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!f_output)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>1;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fprintf(f_output,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;t,x\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Assign<sp/>file<sp/>handle<sp/>to<sp/>network&apos;s<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref>*<sp/>nwk<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork</ref>(f_output);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>fclose(f_output);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>We are now ready to simulate our network using one of the <ref refid="group__network__simulation" kindref="compound">simulation</ref> functions. We will use <ref refid="group__network__simulation_1ga13d5d8530b3b090dba5f9ebd39cb38a7" kindref="member">ndxlNetworkSimulateDopri</ref>, which uses the Dormand-Prince Runge-Kutta pair of order 5(4) to integrate the network agents. Integration starts at the network&apos;s current local simulation time, which is set to <computeroutput>0</computeroutput> by default when we created the network, and we simply specify the duration of the simulation. We can also verify the success of the simulation by checking against <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;stdio.h&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;../include/ndxl.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>main(</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>argc,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal">**<sp/>argv)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__lib__mgmt_1gaf795d2bbc114d928901bc9700830df4e" kindref="member">ndxlInit</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__network__simulation_1ga13d5d8530b3b090dba5f9ebd39cb38a7" kindref="member">ndxlNetworkSimulateDopri</ref>(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>nwk,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Network<sp/>to<sp/>simulate</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>2.5,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Simulation<sp/>duration</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>1e-6,<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Absolute<sp/>tolerance<sp/>(number<sp/>of<sp/>correct<sp/>decimal<sp/>places)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>1e-3,<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Relative<sp/>tolerance<sp/>(number<sp/>of<sp/>correct<sp/>digits)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>NULL,<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Time-stops<sp/>array<sp/>(forced<sp/>evaluation<sp/>times)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>0,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Length<sp/>of<sp/>time-stops<sp/>array<sp/>(must<sp/>be<sp/>0<sp/>if<sp/>time-stops<sp/>is<sp/>NULL)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>cb<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Discrete<sp/>callback<sp/>(called<sp/>once<sp/>at<sp/>t<sp/>=<sp/>0,<sp/>then<sp/>again<sp/>after<sp/>each<sp/>successful<sp/>integration<sp/>step)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Verify<sp/>success</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(result<sp/>==<sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1ga2091f6acf85227ca08a16369595c5bff" kindref="member">ndxlPrintError</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">return</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>If the network successfully simulates, <computeroutput>states.csv</computeroutput> will contain two columns, namely, the evaluated times, and the state of <computeroutput>vert</computeroutput> at those times. We can compare the outputs to the analytical solution of our dynamics function, which is</para>
<para><formula id="16">\[x(t) = \exp{\left(\frac{A}{2}t^2\right)}
\]</formula></para>
<para>given that <formula id="17">$x(t=0)=1$</formula>. We plot the analytical and numerical solutions using a plotting library like <bold><ulink url="https://matplotlib.org/">matplotlib</ulink></bold>.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".py"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">import</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>matplotlib.pyplot<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">as</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>plt</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">import</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>numpy<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">as</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>np</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">#<sp/>Do<sp/>not<sp/>parse<sp/>header<sp/>labels</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t_num,<sp/>x_num<sp/>=<sp/>np.loadtxt(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;states.csv&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>delimiter=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&apos;,&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>skiprows=1,<sp/>unpack=</highlight><highlight class="keyword">True</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">#<sp/>Analyical<sp/>solution</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t_ana<sp/>=<sp/>np.linspace(0.,<sp/>2.5,<sp/>50)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">x_ana<sp/>=<sp/>np.exp(t_ana**2)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">#<sp/>Visualisation</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.plot(t_num,<sp/>x_num,<sp/>label=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Numerical<sp/>solution&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.plot(t_ana,<sp/>x_ana,<sp/>ls=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&apos;--&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>label=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Analytical<sp/>solution&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.xlabel(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Time,<sp/>$t$&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.ylabel(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;$x=f(x,~t)$&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.legend(loc=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;upper<sp/>left&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">plt.savefig(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;states.png&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>bbox_inches=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&apos;tight&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
